    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d104">

                <pb facs="0228" n="140" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg140"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr. Tsui.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-12-08"><hi rendition="#italic">December 8,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose, in further
                    reply to your note of 26th October last, relative to the alleged improper
                    interference of Treasury officials with Chinese residing on Whidbey Island,
                    State of Washington, a copy of letter from the acting Secretary, Mr. Spaulding,
                    and of papers therewith, communicating the result of a special investigation on
                    the subject.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James G. Blaine.</hi></signed></closer>







